Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Keep the FBO colour attachment vectors sized (LP:
 #2160298)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 debian/changelog                              | 10 ++++++
 .../patches/fix-fbo-attachment-arrays.patch   | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 debian/patches/series                         |  1 +
 3 files changed, 43 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 debian/patches/fix-fbo-attachment-arrays.patch

diff --git a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
index feb45ab..11da82e 100644
--- a/debian/changelog
+++ b/debian/changelog
@@ -1,3 +1,13 @@
+nux (4.0.8+18.10.20180623-0ubuntu15+unity2) resolute; urgency=medium
+
+  * debian/patches/fix-fbo-attachment-arrays.patch: keep the FBO colour
+    attachment vectors sized. FormatFrameBufferObject() cleared them right
+    after SetupFrameBufferObject() sized them, so every attachment call
+    indexed an empty vector: an abort under -D_GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS, and the
+    attached textures were never released. (LP: #2160298)
+
+ -- Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>  Thu, 24 Sep 2026 23:36:00 +0000
+
 nux (4.0.8+18.10.20180623-0ubuntu15+unity1) resolute; urgency=medium
 
   * Rebuild upstream 0ubuntu15 (stonking) for resolute.
diff --git a/debian/patches/fix-fbo-attachment-arrays.patch b/debian/patches/fix-fbo-attachment-arrays.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3953001
--- /dev/null
+++ b/debian/patches/fix-fbo-attachment-arrays.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Description: Keep the FBO colour attachment vectors sized
+ IOpenGLFrameBufferObject::SetupFrameBufferObject() sizes
+ texture_attachment_array_ and surface_attachment_array_ to
+ GetMaxFboAttachment() and then calls FormatFrameBufferObject(), which
+ clear()s both. Every later SetRenderTarget(), SetTextureAttachment(),
+ TextureAttachment() and Activate() indexes the now empty vectors: undefined
+ behaviour that happens to work (the capacity is still there), aborts under
+ -D_GLIBCXX_ASSERTIONS, and never releases the attachments' references, since
+ the vector's destructor sees no elements. Reset the elements instead.
+Author: Ubuntu Unity Life Support <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
+Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/nux/+bug/2160298
+Forwarded: no
+Last-Update: 2026-09-24
+---
+--- a/NuxGraphics/IOpenGLFrameBufferObject.cpp
++++ b/NuxGraphics/IOpenGLFrameBufferObject.cpp
+@@ -69,8 +69,13 @@ namespace nux
+   {
+     Deactivate();
+ 
+-    texture_attachment_array_.clear();
+-    surface_attachment_array_.clear();
++    // Drop the attachments but keep one slot per colour attachment:
++    // SetRenderTarget(), SetTextureAttachment(), TextureAttachment() and
++    // Activate() index these vectors up to GetMaxFboAttachment().
++    for (auto& texture : texture_attachment_array_)
++      texture = ObjectPtr<IOpenGLBaseTexture> (0);
++    for (auto& surface : surface_attachment_array_)
++      surface = ObjectPtr<IOpenGLSurface> (0);
+ 
+     depth_surface_attachment_ = ObjectPtr<IOpenGLSurface> (0);
+     stencil_surface_attachment_ = ObjectPtr<IOpenGLSurface> (0);
diff --git a/debian/patches/series b/debian/patches/series
index a4851c1..47d3a6b 100644
--- a/debian/patches/series
+++ b/debian/patches/series
@@ -6,3 +6,4 @@ disable-TestLoggingWriter-test.diff
 boost1.90.patch
 remove_unicode_licensed.patch
 fix-missing-vidmode.patch
+fix-fbo-attachment-arrays.patch
